WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.427
One observation is rarely enough in analytics.

00:00:03.427 --> 00:00:07.692
We usually want to work with a sequence of related values.

00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:12.527
A list is ordered and mutable, meaning we can change it.

00:00:12.527 --> 00:00:17.437
A tuple is ordered too, but it is intended to remain fixed.

00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:21.708
An index gives us a position number for accessing one value.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.297
Think about five exam scores or a week of daily sales.

00:00:26.297 --> 00:00:34.065
A sequence lets us store those values together and then summarize, filter, or process them as one collection.
